| Regulatory literacy | Reads EU and Dutch law and implementation directly; four books of it (CRA, Data Act, DPP, GTO, EUDI, machinery) | Compliance as a moat in distribution or services; sees deadlines before the market | Not legal advice; counsel still needed |
| Engineering habit | Automates, integrates, measures; systems thinking | Operations that others run on spreadsheets and WhatsApp; evidence trails | Must not become an IT business again |
| Research pipeline | The book machine: evidence-led screening, panel review, verdicts | Can screen 10 options for the cost of one consultant's afternoon | Screening is not selling |
| Audience | ~30,000 LinkedIn followers, professional | A channel for B2B offers, recruiting partners, testing demand | Not a consumer channel; not to be turned into a content business |
| Constraints | A2 Dutch; day job (?); family (?); risk appetite (?); retraining tolerance (?) | | The four open constraints: passive vs hands-on; alongside the job or replacing it; capital ceiling; two years of retraining or not |
