@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 <main class="wrap">
 <p class="kicker">Essay 3 of 6 · The joinery and steel dossier · from pitch 6</p>
 <h1>The file is valuable only when it is missing</h1>
-<p class="lede">A small Dutch builder can buy windows from Poland and save money on the object, then lose the saving while matching declarations, performance values and installation evidence to a live project. The proposed business closes that gap in Polish and hands the builder a Dutch-ready evidence pack. Yet the strongest official guidance says correct manufacturer instructions may already give the quality assurer sufficient proof. <!-- CHECK: 03-product-evidence --> Large factories publish documents and sell through distributors. <!-- CHECK: 03-eko-incumbent --> The purchase decision is therefore not “does Wkb create paperwork?” It is whether a builder importing directly will pay a separate fee before one incomplete order delays approval or creates rework.</p>
+<p class="lede">A small Dutch builder can buy windows from Poland and save money on the object, then lose the saving while matching declarations, performance values and installation evidence to a live project. The proposed business closes that gap in Polish and hands the builder a Dutch-ready evidence pack. Yet official guidance says installation according to the manufacturer’s instructions can itself give the quality assurer sufficient proof. <!-- CHECK: 03-product-evidence --> Eko-Okna markets a Dutch business contact, distributor platform and document library. <!-- CHECK: 03-eko-incumbent --> Those are useful incumbent surfaces, not proof that a specific order’s Dutch project file is complete. The purchase decision is whether an importing builder will pay separately to close that gap.</p>
 
 <section class="proposition">
 <h2>The proposition</h2>
@@ -37,8 +37,8 @@
 <section class="changed">
 <h2>What changed</h2>
 <p>The Wkb rules began on 1 January 2024 for new buildings in consequence class 1. That class includes ground-level homes and certain simple industrial buildings. Renovation remains postponed without a fixed start date, and higher consequence classes await evaluation. <!-- CHECK: 03-wkb-scope --> This is a narrow trigger, not a mandate covering every replacement-window job.</p>
-<p>For a covered project, the quality assurer checks the work during construction and issues a statement when there is justified confidence that the building meets the technical rules. Before use, the client submits a completion notification. The authority receives the assurer’s statement plus specified information on risks, structure, ventilation, energy, environmental performance, fire safety and equivalent measures. An incomplete notification prevents the two-week clock to lawful use from starting. <!-- CHECK: 03-completion-dossier --></p>
-<p>That “dossier bevoegd gezag” is not a sack containing every certificate for every product. The private consumer or handover dossier is also distinct. It includes drawings, calculations, materials, installations, functions and use and maintenance information. The municipality and quality assurer are not parties to that private dossier, although some material can be reused for the completion notification. <!-- CHECK: 03-consumer-dossier --></p>
+<p>During construction, the quality assurer executes the assurance plan, monitors the work and reports conflicts to the contractor and client. It also informs the municipality if problems remain unresolved. After construction, it issues a statement if it finds everything in order. Before use, the client submits that statement with the completion notification and specified technical information. An incomplete notification prevents the two-week clock to lawful use from starting. <!-- CHECK: 03-completion-dossier --></p>
+<p>That “dossier bevoegd gezag” is not a sack containing every certificate for every product. The private consumer or handover dossier is also distinct. It includes drawings, calculations, materials, installations, functions and use and maintenance information. The municipality and quality assurer are not parties to that private dossier. <!-- CHECK: 03-consumer-dossier --></p>
 <p>Construction-product rules still create real inputs. Dutch government guidance names windows as construction products and says a Declaration of Performance is mandatory, with the manufacturer stating the product’s performance. <!-- CHECK: 03-cpr-duty --> TloKB adds the operational point: where a builder installs a product according to the manufacturer’s instructions, that can be sufficient evidence of product performance and processing. A deviation can require the builder to provide its own substantiation. <!-- CHECK: 03-product-evidence --> The opportunity sits in matching and exceptions, not inventing certificates.</p>
 <p>There is a substantial physical corridor. Eurostat reports 2025 Dutch imports from Poland of €160.0 million under HS 7308 iron or steel structures and parts, and €148.3 million under HS 7610 aluminium structures and parts. Both headings include far more than the proposed window orders. <!-- CHECK: 03-trade-flow --> They prove goods move, not that Dutch builders bought them directly, that files were deficient or that a separate budget exists.</p>
 <p>CBAM should leave the launch offer. The definitive regime began on 1 January 2026 and applies to EU importers bringing covered goods into the EU. The current single mass threshold is more than 50 tonnes, with iron, steel and aluminium among the sectors. <!-- CHECK: 03-cbam --> A Polish-to-Dutch movement is intra-EU. Any CBAM duty arose at the external EU border, so a Dutch joinery dossier should not casually promise a new CBAM filing for each Polish order. <!-- CHECK: 03-cbam-boundary --></p>
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 <h2>Why you</h2>
 <p>Polish does useful work on the supply side. The founder can challenge a quotation, obtain a product-specific declaration, resolve conflicting identifiers and ask a factory engineer why the installation instruction differs from the drawing. Regulatory literacy keeps the request tied to the project requirement. The engineering habit turns messages and PDFs into a controlled acceptance record.</p>
 <p>The Dutch gate is not an exam; it is the customer channel. <!-- CHECK: 03-language-gate --> The buyer, site supervisor and quality assurer discuss risk, deviations and responsibility in Dutch. A2 is not enough for a disputed site meeting or a sales call about liability. From the first paid order, a Dutch-speaking construction-quality consultant must lead those meetings under a fixed fee. The founder keeps the contract and the Polish factory relationship. If no credible consultant accepts that boundary, the channel fails.</p>
-<p>FENBRO is the closest precedent found elsewhere. Its site describes selling Polish joinery abroad and a complete Irish service of product, delivery, installation and warranty. It identifies its company at Ludna 2/320 in Warsaw. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-model --> Companies House independently records a same-named FENBRO LTD with two Polish directors at 2 Lok. 320, Ludna in Warsaw. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-trace --> An April 2026 accounts filing describes the UK company as dormant through March 2026. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-dormant --> That is a trace, not proof of attractive economics. More importantly, FENBRO sells the whole transaction. No independently traced small firm was found whose principal product is a separately priced dossier. <!-- CHECK: 03-precedent-gap --></p>
+<p>FENBRO is the closest precedent found elsewhere. Its site describes selling Polish joinery abroad and a complete Irish service of product, delivery, installation and warranty. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-model --> Poland’s official KRS registers FENBRO Sp. z o.o. as KRS 0000947765 at Ludna 2/320 in Warsaw. Its registered activities include joinery installation and agents selling building materials. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-krs --> Companies House records a same-named FENBRO LTD with two Polish directors at that Warsaw address. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-trace --> An April 2026 filing describes the UK company as dormant through March 2026. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-dormant --> The records show a shared name and address, but do not state a parent, subsidiary or ownership relationship. <!-- CHECK: 03-fenbro-relationship --> The Polish registration is the independent entity trace; the UK company is only corroboration. Neither proves attractive economics. More importantly, FENBRO sells the whole transaction. No independently traced small firm was found whose principal product is a separately priced dossier. <!-- CHECK: 03-precedent-gap --></p>
 <p>The edge breaks if the reader will not work through a Dutch lead or cannot visit projects during business hours. A perfect Polish supplier call does not replace a Dutch conversation when the quality assurer flags an exception.</p>
 </section>
 
